d before contacting the maintainer directly.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUbuntu Manpage: AppArmor - kernel enhancement to confine programs to a limited set of resources. (https://manpages.ubuntu.com/manpages/noble/man7/apparmor.7.html)\nciteturn97search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today;   * Provided by: apparmor (Version: 4.0.1really4.0.1-0ubuntu0.24.04.9)\n\n# AppArmor\n\nkernel enhancement to confine programs to a limited set of resources.\n\n  * Provided by: apparmor (Version: 4.0.1really4.0.1-0ubuntu0.24.04.9)\n\nAppArmor is a kernel enhancement to confine programs to a limited set of resources. AppArmor's unique security model is to bind access control attributes to programs rather than to users.\n\nAppArmor confinement is provided via profiles loaded into the kernel via apparmor_parser(8), typically through the apparmor.service systemd unit, which is used like this:\n    \n            # systemctl start apparmor\n            # systemctl reload apparmor\n    \n\nAppArmor can operate in two modes: enforcement, and complain or learning:\n\n  * enforcement - Profiles loaded in enforcement mode will result in enforcement of the policy defined in the profile as well as reporting policy violation attempts to syslogd.\n  * complain - Profiles loaded in \"complain\" mode will not enforce policy. Instead, it will report policy violation attempts. This mode is convenient for developing profiles. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUbuntu – Details of source package linux-hwe-7.0 in noble-updates (https://packages.ubuntu.com/eu/source/noble-updates/amd64/linux-hwe-7.0)\nciteturn97search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; # Source Package: linux-hwe-7.0 (7.0.0-42.42~24.04.1)\n\n# Source Package: linux-hwe-7.0 (7.0.0-42.42~24.04.1)\n\n## Links for linux-hwe-7.0\n\n### Ubuntu Resources:\n\n  * Bug Reports\n  * Ubuntu Changelog\n  * Copyright File\n\n### Maintainer:\n\n  